# Koa Routing And Repositories

- Mount new HTTP surfaces through `Routes/unprotected-repositories.js` or `Routes/protected-repositories.js`; adding a route file alone is not enough.
- Preserve `server.js` boot order: unprotected routes before `koa-jwt`, protected routes after it.
- Match the existing repository shape under `Repositories/<Feature>/` and keep business logic out of route declarations.
- Prefer the backend flow `route -> controller -> module -> model/middleware`.
- If an older script or note mentions `api.routes.js`, treat that as stale and use the `Routes/*-repositories.js` registries instead.

## Examples

```js
// Prefer
require("../Repositories/Tags/routes/tags.routes")(server);
```

